  <static seed="1928" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers40.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p>Do not use a calculator.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{49} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{0.49} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{4900} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.7</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>70</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>First, recognize that <m>49</m> is a square number. Since <m>7\cdot7=49</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{49}=7</m>.</p>
<p>Next, since <m>0.7\cdot0.7=0.49</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{0.49}=0.7</m>.</p>
<p>Finally, since <m>70\cdot70=4900</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{4900}=70</m>.</p>
</solution>
